{"asked":[{"category":"roles","difference":"D-8","id":"Q-1","impact":3,"impactReason":"Roles control who can write operational records and who can see potentially sensitive cost and performance information.","options":["No role distinctions; all users can view and operate all product areas.","Use a small built-in set of roles, such as administrator, operator, and viewer, with cost/performance access controlled by role.","Define configurable roles and per-action permissions, including record-level access to yards, lots, and pens."],"reason":"No roles or restricted audiences are required by the request, so a shared access model is the smallest implementation.","recommended":"No role distinctions; all users can view and operate all product areas.","score":9,"spans":["I-1","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","I-8","I-9","I-10"],"text":"Which user roles and access boundaries are required for operational records, cost/performance views, imports, and data entry?","topic":"roles","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","difference":"D-3","id":"Q-2","impact":3,"impactReason":"The choice changes stock balances and whether wastage is counted once or potentially twice.","options":["Apply the ratio to consumption estimates and projections; record actual wastage separately only when entered as a movement.","Treat the ratio as the actual wastage movement and decrement stock by it whenever feed is consumed.","Apply the ratio to estimates and projections, and also let users record actual wastage movements separately."],"reason":"This avoids inventing actual losses while supporting the requested configurable forecast adjustment.","recommended":"Apply the ratio to consumption estimates and projections; record actual wastage separately only when entered as a movement.","score":9,"spans":["I-3"],"text":"Should the wastage ratio represent only forecasted/estimated losses, or should actual wastage also be recorded as a separate stock movement?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-3","impact":3,"impactReason":"Attribution directly changes lot feed consumption, feed cost, FCR, and cost of gain.","options":["Require the operator to enter a separate activity quantity for each affected lot.","Allocate the pen's actual quantity and cost among its lots in proportion to animal count at the time of feeding.","Attribute the full pen activity to one selected lot; record separate activities for other lots."],"reason":"Explicit lot quantities avoid double-counting and do not assume that every lot received the same amount per animal.","recommended":"Require the operator to enter a separate activity quantity for each affected lot.","score":9,"spans":["I-5","I-7","I-8"],"text":"When one pen contains multiple lots, how should a feeding activity's actual quantity and cost be attributed to lot-level metrics?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-4","impact":3,"impactReason":"The basis changes reported feed consumption and the resulting FCR values.","options":["Use as-fed pounds for total feed consumed and FCR, converting entered inventory units to pounds as needed.","Convert feed to dry-matter pounds using each ingredient's dry-matter percentage before calculating FCR.","Show both as-fed and dry-matter FCR."],"reason":"The request defines total feed consumed in pounds and does not require a dry-matter-adjusted metric.","recommended":"Use as-fed pounds for total feed consumed and FCR, converting entered inventory units to pounds as needed.","score":9,"spans":["I-3","I-4","I-5","I-7","I-9"],"text":"Should feed-to-gain calculations use feed on an as-fed basis or adjust feed consumption to dry matter?","topic":"terminology","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-5","impact":3,"impactReason":"A full ROI calculation adds financial inputs and could materially change profitability claims.","options":["Report feed cost per pound of gain only; do not label it full ROI or profitability.","Calculate full lot ROI using purchase cost, feed cost, sale proceeds, and any other specified operating costs.","Show feed cost and procurement cost, but omit ROI until sale proceeds and other costs are available."],"reason":"Feed cost per gain is explicitly defined; full ROI needs sale proceeds and additional cost inputs not specified in the request.","recommended":"Report feed cost per pound of gain only; do not label it full ROI or profitability.","score":9,"spans":["I-1","I-7","I-8"],"text":"Does 'lot-level profitability/ROI' require more than the specified feed cost per unit of weight gain?","topic":"reporting","uncertainty":3}],"assumptions":[{"fromQuestion":"Q1","fromSpan":["I-1","I-10"],"id":"ASM-1","risk":"high","text":"How should procurement and receiving data connect to the primary procurement system for this build? → assumed: Use clearly labelled mock/source data only; no live connector is required."},{"fromQuestion":"Q2","fromSpan":["I-1"],"id":"ASM-2","risk":"high","text":"What should happen when an import contains duplicate source identifiers, an unmatched PO line or lot, or a lot-to-pen assignment exceeding capacity? → assumed: Report row-level problems, keep unmatched records out of downstream pen operations, reject over-capacity assignments, and prevent duplicate imports from double-counting records."},{"fromQuestion":"Q3","fromSpan":["I-2","I-7"],"id":"ASM-3","risk":"low","text":"Which gain-rate assumption should drive projected market dates when current lot performance is unavailable or differs from the configured assumption? → assumed: Use the lot's current measured ADG whenever available, falling back to a configured default only when it is unavailable."},{"fromQuestion":"Q5","fromSpan":["I-3"],"id":"ASM-4","risk":"low","text":"Should inventory projections also flag items expected to run low or out of stock within the selected horizon? → assumed: Show projected balances only; do not add low-stock alerts."},{"fromQuestion":"Q6","fromSpan":["I-4"],"id":"ASM-5","risk":"low","text":"What objective and constraints should ration optimization use to identify economical mixes? → assumed: Compare ingredient mixes by cost and recorded nutrition values; users specify nutritional targets or constraints for a lowest-cost feasible comparison."},{"fromQuestion":"Q7","fromSpan":["I-5"],"id":"ASM-6","risk":"low","text":"Must each actual feeding activity be linked to an existing dated plan, or may operators record an activity without one? → assumed: Make the plan link optional, while showing whether each activity was planned or unplanned."},{"fromQuestion":"Q9","fromSpan":["I-5","I-6","I-7"],"id":"ASM-7","risk":"high","text":"How should a recorded weight or feeding event be corrected after it has affected inventory or lot metrics? → assumed: Allow authorized users to edit or delete the event, then recalculate affected balances and metrics."},{"fromQuestion":"Q12","fromSpan":["I-7","I-9"],"id":"ASM-8","risk":"low","text":"What should the report's date-range filter refer to when comparing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain? → assumed: Use the date range to select the latest weight reading in that period and feeding events up to that reading."},{"fromQuestion":"Q14","fromSpan":["I-10"],"id":"ASM-9","risk":"high","text":"How should users access the sample dataset, and what should happen if sample records conflict with operational records? → assumed: Provide a clearly labelled, separate demo dataset that users can load on demand; report conflicts and avoid presenting a partial load as complete."},{"fromQuestion":"Q15","fromSpan":["I-11"],"id":"ASM-10","risk":"low","text":"Should the demo/project area include an overview of the prompts used to build the solution, in addition to the requested testing, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market material? → assumed: Omit prompt history; include the requested demo, testing/validation, challenges, production-readiness, and go-to-market material."}],"conflicts":[],"differences":[{"id":"D-1","readings":[{"behaviour":1,"sketch":1,"summary":"Tracks PO-line-to-lot splits with assigned quantities and traceability, but does not specify permissions, unmatched-record handling, or capacity enforcement."},{"behaviour":3,"sketch":2,"summary":"Restricts import and mapping to authorized users; unauthorized users can only view permitted data."},{"behaviour":5,"sketch":2,"summary":"Keeps unmapped records out of pen operations and rejects or flags over-capacity assignments."},{"behaviour":4,"sketch":3,"summary":"Identifies duplicate imports and avoids silently double-counting animals, receipts, or costs."}],"span":"I-1","topic":"Procurement import and mapping controls"},{"id":"D-2","readings":[{"behaviour":1,"sketch":1,"summary":"Refreshes forecasts using current weight-gain performance when available."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":2,"summary":"Uses a configured gain assumption for the projected target-weight date."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"Lets users update and retain a target weight or ADG assumption with the forecast."}],"span":"I-2","topic":"Forecast assumptions and gain-rate source"},{"id":"D-3","readings":[{"behaviour":1,"sketch":1,"summary":"Records opening stock, receipts, consumption, wastage, and closing stock as identifiable movements."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":2,"summary":"Records receipts, adjustments, and wastage as dated, attributable movements."},{"behaviour":3,"sketch":2,"summary":"Flags items projected to run low or out of stock within a selected horizon."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"Records receipts, consumption, or adjustments as dated movements and updates applicable cost totals."}],"span":"I-3","topic":"Inventory movement types and forecast alerts"},{"id":"D-4","readings":[{"behaviour":2,"sketch":1,"summary":"Compares mixes and identifies economical alternatives for the intended animal or weight range."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Presents economical candidates for a specified feeding objective and requires an authorized user to select a suggestion before applying it to pens."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":3,"summary":"Optimizes for user-specified nutritional targets or constraints and presents feasible mixes with estimated costs."}],"span":"I-4","topic":"Ration optimization objective and applying suggestions"},{"id":"D-5","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Generates or creates a dated pen plan and includes planned quantity, per-animal quantity, feeding time, cost, energy, and status."},{"behaviour":5,"sketch":2,"summary":"Restricts plan creation and activity entry by permission and limits operators to authorized pens and operations."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"Records actual feeding against a pen and plan, whereas the other readings permit activities to be entered against a pen and date without requiring an explicit plan."}],"span":"I-5","topic":"Feeding authorization and execution requirements"},{"id":"D-6","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Records lot weight measurements and calculates gain when prior readings are comparable."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":2,"summary":"Requires authorized entry and retains readings append-only, with attributable corrections rather than silent history replacement."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Rejects invalid readings with field-level explanations and identifies out-of-order dates."},{"behaviour":3,"sketch":3,"summary":"Flags inconsistent counts or readings predating the prior reading to protect the time series."}],"span":"I-6","topic":"Weight-history correction and validation"},{"id":"D-7","readings":[{"behaviour":1,"sketch":1,"summary":"Defines FCR from feed consumed and gain, and cost of gain from feed cost and gain."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Makes source readings and feeding events underlying each metric inspectable for reconciliation."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":3,"summary":"Projects ship date from current weight, target weight, days on feed, and ADG, and displays the projection inputs."}],"span":"I-7","topic":"Metric inputs, auditability, and ship-date calculation"},{"id":"D-8","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Provides broad operational dashboard and report metrics without specifying role-based restrictions."},{"behaviour":4,"sketch":2,"summary":"Restricts dashboard and report details to records permitted by the user's access."}],"span":"I-8","topic":"Dashboard access controls"},{"id":"D-9","readings":[{"behaviour":1,"sketch":1,"summary":"Specifies date, breed, sex, and pen filters but no access restrictions or invalid-filter handling."},{"behaviour":3,"sketch":2,"summary":"Identifies invalid date ranges and unsupported filter values rather than applying them."},{"behaviour":4,"sketch":2,"summary":"Prevents users lacking report access from viewing or exporting restricted performance and financial data."}],"span":"I-9","topic":"Report access controls and invalid-filter handling"},{"id":"D-10","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Provides coherent sample records but does not specify a user-triggered loading workflow or duplicate behavior."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":2,"summary":"Lets a user load a coherent sample dataset to demonstrate connected workflows."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Reports whether repeated sample loading added, found already-present, or could not load records, avoiding silent duplicates."},{"behaviour":3,"sketch":2,"summary":"Reports conflicts or load failures and avoids presenting a partial load as complete."}],"span":"I-10","topic":"Sample-data loading and duplicate/conflict handling"},{"id":"D-11","readings":[{"behaviour":2,"sketch":1,"summary":"Requires testing/validation overview, challenges, and production-readiness assessment, but does not specify a prompts overview."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":2,"summary":"Includes an overview of prompts used in addition to demo, testing, challenges, and readiness content."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":3,"summary":"Requires testing/validation and challenges or limitations, with production-readiness assessment stated separately."}],"span":"I-11","topic":"Demo-area content and evaluation scope"}],"round":1,"sketches":[{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Import procurement and receiving records containing vendor, costs, head count, weights, and animal details; show the imported records and their resulting lot and pen mappings."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Allow a PO line to be associated with one lot or split across multiple lots, and associate lots with physical pens, including pen ID, capacity, and current animal count; retain traceability from each lot and pen back to its PO line and receiving data."},{"kind":"error","text":"When an import or mapping has missing, invalid, or conflicting identifiers or quantities, show which records could not be processed and why, and do not silently create incomplete or inconsistent mappings."},{"kind":"data","text":"When a PO line is split among lots, retain the source relationship and the quantities assigned to each lot so downstream lot-level costs and performance can be traced to procurement."}],"id":"I-1"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Use incoming animal and receiving data, including entry weight and receiving date, to calculate and display a projected market/ship date and target weight for the lot."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Recalculate and display the forecast when relevant animal or lot data changes, using current weight-gain performance when available."},{"kind":"error","text":"If required inputs such as entry weight, receiving date, target weight, or a usable gain rate are absent or invalid, indicate that a reliable forecast cannot be calculated instead of showing a misleading date."}],"id":"I-2"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Let users view and maintain feed inventory items with feed type, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location."},{"kind":"data","text":"Record opening stock, receipts, consumption, wastage, and closing stock as identifiable movements, and update the displayed available quantity when stock is received or consumed."},{"kind":"data","text":"Apply the configured wastage ratio to consumption estimates and projected inventory needs; let users view projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons."},{"kind":"error","text":"When a movement would produce invalid quantities, such as a negative quantity or consumption beyond available stock, show the issue and prevent a misleading stock balance from being recorded."},{"kind":"error","text":"Show when forecasts depend on missing or stale movement, usage, or wastage data, rather than presenting an unsupported projection as certain."}],"id":"I-3"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Let users create and edit a named ration with its type, intended animal type or weight range, ingredients, and a quantity or proportion for each ingredient."},{"kind":"data","text":"For each ration, display the calculated ingredient-based cost per unit and nutritional values, including dry matter and energy, where ingredient data is available."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Let users compare candidate ingredient mixes by nutritional values and cost, and identify economical alternatives for the intended animal or weight range."},{"kind":"error","text":"If ingredient proportions or quantities are invalid, required ingredient prices or nutrition values are unavailable, or a mix cannot be calculated, identify the affected ration and metric rather than reporting a false total."}],"id":"I-4"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Generate or let users create a dated feeding plan for a physical pen using its animal count, daily bunk rate, selected ration, and assigned lot; show planned quantity, quantity per animal, feeding time, estimated cost and energy, and plan status."},{"kind":"data","text":"Let users record a feeding activity against a pen, lot, and ration with planned and actual quantities; show the calculated variance as actual minus planned and the feeding status."},{"kind":"data","text":"On recording actual feeding, calculate the event's feed cost and energy, consume inventory according to the ration's ingredient mix, and update lot-level cumulative feed consumption and feed cost."},{"kind":"error","text":"If actual feeding exceeds available inventory or required pen, lot, ration, or quantity data is missing or invalid, show the problem and do not silently record inconsistent inventory or feeding totals."},{"kind":"data","text":"Allow a pen to contain animals from one or more lots and associate feeding records with the applicable lot or lots so pen execution and lot-level results remain attributable."}],"id":"I-5"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Let users record a lot weight measurement with measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, and notes; calculate or display weight gain since the prior reading when comparable readings exist."},{"kind":"data","text":"Retain dated weight readings for each lot and display them as a time series so users can inspect weight trends over time."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a measurement is missing required values, contains invalid quantities, or cannot be compared with a prior reading, identify the issue and avoid presenting an unsupported weight-gain value."}],"id":"I-6"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"For each lot, calculate and display days on feed from receiving date, total weight gain from entry and current average weights, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date."},{"kind":"data","text":"Use total feed consumed in pounds divided by total weight gain in pounds for FCR, and total feed cost divided by total weight gain for cost of gain; use the lot's recorded feeding and weight events as the inputs."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Recalculate affected lot metrics when a feeding event or weight measurement is recorded or changed, and reflect the updated values in the lot's performance view."},{"kind":"error","text":"If weight gain is zero or negative, dates or weights are unavailable, or average daily gain cannot support a ship-date forecast, mark the affected metric unavailable or not meaningful rather than dividing by zero or presenting a misleading result."}],"id":"I-7"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Provide dashboards and reports that show lot, pen, ration, inventory, feeding, and performance information, including active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, planned versus actual feed, consumption and cost, starting and current weight, weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain/FCR, cost per gain, and energy consumed."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Let operators identify and compare high- and low-performing lots and answer operational questions such as which pen consumed the most feed, which ration is used most, whether actual feeding matches plan, and which pens are over- or underfed."},{"kind":"data","text":"Provide a yard-level summary across active lots showing aggregate head count, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost."},{"kind":"error","text":"When a view has no matching or sufficient data, show an empty or unavailable state instead of fabricated metrics."}],"id":"I-8"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Provide a dedicated feed-to-gain report comparing ADG, FCR, and cost of gain across lots."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Let users filter report results by date range, breed, sex, and pen, and update the displayed comparison to match the selected filters."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Let users export the filtered report as CSV or PDF, with the exported results corresponding to the displayed filters and metrics."},{"kind":"error","text":"If filters return no lots or required values are unavailable, indicate that clearly; if an export cannot be generated, show an error rather than returning an incomplete file as successful."}],"id":"I-9"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Provide clearly identified sample/mock records for procurement and receiving, lots, pens, animals, inventory and stock movements, rations, feeding plans and activities, and weight measurements so the end-to-end system can be demonstrated."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Ensure sample records have coherent relationships and values that can drive inventory, forecasts, lot metrics, dashboards, and report examples."},{"kind":"data","text":"Clearly distinguish sample/mock records from operational records so users are not misled into treating demonstration data as actual business activity."}],"id":"I-10"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Provide a proposed solution and architecture diagrams describing the feedlot data flow and how procurement, lots, pens, inventory, rations, feeding, weights, and performance reporting relate."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Provide a demonstrable responsive web app covering the proposed feedlot workflows on phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths."},{"kind":"data","text":"Provide an overview of testing and validation performed, including how feed-to-gain calculations and data consistency were checked, and describe challenges encountered and the assessed degree of production readiness."},{"kind":"data","text":"Provide a go-to-market strategy and analysis for the proposed product offering."}],"id":"I-11"}]},{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"An authorized user imports procurement and receiving records containing vendor, costs, head count, weights, and source identifiers; the system creates or updates the corresponding records and shows an import summary of accepted, rejected, and unmatched rows."},{"kind":"data","text":"Users can map a PO line to one or more lots and associate lots with pens; each mapping retains its source identifiers so users can navigate between PO line, lot, and pen and see the origin of procurement and receiving values."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system records pen capacity and current animal count from the source and makes lot/pen associations available to downstream feeding and performance views."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users without import or mapping permission cannot import or alter these records; they can only view information permitted by their access."},{"kind":"error","text":"Rows with missing required values, invalid quantities, unknown references, or conflicting duplicate source identifiers are reported with row-level reasons and are not silently treated as valid; users can correct and retry them."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a PO line or lot cannot yet be mapped to a pen, the record remains visibly unmatched and is excluded from pen-level operations until mapped; an attempted over-capacity assignment is rejected or flagged for correction."}],"id":"I-1","readingChosen":"Treat procurement/receiving ingestion as importing source PO and receipt records into the web app, then maintaining explicit PO-line → lot → pen traceability, including one PO line split across multiple lots."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"On receipt of valid incoming animal data, the system displays a target weight and projected date at which the lot is expected to reach it, using the lot's entry weight, receiving date, target weight, and configured gain assumption."},{"kind":"data","text":"Users can review or change permitted forecast inputs, and the displayed projection updates to reflect the changed inputs; the inputs and resulting forecast are associated with the lot."},{"kind":"error","text":"When required inputs are missing or invalid, the system identifies which values are needed and does not present a misleading projected date or target weight."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the lot's current or assumed gain is zero or negative, the system indicates that a meaningful market-date projection is unavailable rather than dividing by zero or projecting a false date."}],"id":"I-2","readingChosen":"Treat the forecast as a projection derived from received animal weight and receiving date plus a configured target weight and gain assumption, not as a guaranteed sale date."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can view inventory by feed item, category, quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location, together with opening stock, receipts, consumption, and closing stock for a selected period."},{"kind":"data","text":"Authorized users record receipts, adjustments, and wastage; each movement updates the item balance and remains visible as a dated, attributable stock movement."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can set a wastage ratio; consumption estimates and inventory projections include that ratio and show the resulting forecast balances for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The system flags items projected to run low or out of stock within a selected horizon so users can act before planned feeding is affected."},{"kind":"error","text":"A movement that would create an invalid negative balance, uses an incompatible unit, or has invalid quantity or cost is rejected with an explanation; users can correct it rather than having inventory silently diverge."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users without inventory-edit permission may view permitted balances and forecasts but cannot record receipts, adjustments, or wastage."}],"id":"I-3","readingChosen":"Treat inventory forecasts as projections for each requested horizon—daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, half-year, and annual—based on current stock, recorded movements, planned or observed consumption, and configurable wastage."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Authorized users create and edit rations with a name, type, ingredients, ingredient quantities or proportions, dry-matter and energy values, unit cost, and intended animal type or weight range."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system calculates the ration's ingredient-derived cost per unit and aggregate nutritional values and displays the contribution of each ingredient."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users compare alternative ration mixes on cost and nutritional values and can view an economical candidate for the specified feeding objective; a suggested mix is not applied to pens until an authorized user selects it."},{"kind":"error","text":"The system rejects or flags a ration with missing ingredients, invalid quantities, proportions that do not make a complete mix, or unavailable ingredient cost/nutrient data; it does not report a misleading calculated cost or nutrition total."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users without ration-edit permission can view available rations and comparisons but cannot change or activate a ration."}],"id":"I-4","readingChosen":"Treat ration optimization as a comparison of feasible ingredient mixes using their recorded nutritional values and costs, with the user choosing whether to apply a suggested mix."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"An authorized user generates or edits a dated plan for a pen from its animal count, daily bunk rate, selected ration, and feeding time; the system displays planned quantity, quantity per animal, expected energy intake, and estimated total cost."},{"kind":"data","text":"The plan records its pen, assigned lot where applicable, animal count, ration, planned quantity, date, time, and status (Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped), and is available to operators for that pen and date."},{"kind":"happy","text":"An operator records a feeding activity against a pen and date, including lot, ration, planned and actual quantities, variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, and status; the system shows actual-versus-planned variance as actual quantity minus planned quantity."},{"kind":"data","text":"On saving a valid activity, the system consumes the corresponding ingredient quantities from inventory, calculates and records feed cost and energy, and updates cumulative lot feed and cost totals."},{"kind":"error","text":"The system blocks or clearly reports an activity with missing/invalid pen, ration, date, or quantity, or insufficient ingredient stock; it does not silently post a partial inventory decrement or falsely mark the activity completed."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users without feeding-plan or activity-entry permission cannot create plans or log actual feed; permitted operators can enter activities only for the pens and operations they are authorized to access."}],"id":"I-5","readingChosen":"Treat a feed plan as a dated pen-level instruction that may assign a lot within a pen, and a feeding activity as the separately recorded actual execution against that plan."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"An authorized user records a lot, measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, and notes; the system derives or displays weight gain since the previous valid reading."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system retains dated lot readings and displays them chronologically so users can inspect weight and gain trends over time."},{"kind":"error","text":"A reading with missing lot/date, nonpositive animal count, or invalid weight is rejected with a field-level explanation; an out-of-order date is identified and does not produce a misleading gain calculation."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users without weight-entry permission can view permitted reading history but cannot add or correct measurements."}],"id":"I-6","readingChosen":"Treat each lot weight measurement as a dated reading that is retained in an append-only time series; corrections are attributable rather than silently replacing history."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"For each lot, the system calculates days on feed from receiving date, total weight gain from current average weight minus entry average weight, ADG from gain divided by days on feed, cumulative feed consumed, FCR, and feed cost per pound of gain from cumulative feed cost divided by gain."},{"kind":"happy","text":"After a valid feeding activity, the lot's cumulative feed and cost and derived efficiency metrics refresh; after a valid weight measurement, current weight, gain, ADG, FCR, and cost of gain refresh."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system makes the input readings and feeding events underlying each lot metric inspectable so users can reconcile the displayed calculation."},{"kind":"error","text":"If there is no valid weight gain, no elapsed days, or incomplete source data, affected ratios or rates are shown as unavailable with the reason rather than as zero, infinity, or a misleading value."},{"kind":"error","text":"If an event is rejected or fails validation, it does not update the lot's derived metrics or cumulative totals."}],"id":"I-7","readingChosen":"Use the stated feed-to-gain definitions: FCR is cumulative feed consumed in pounds divided by total lot weight gain in pounds, and recalculate lot metrics after valid feeding or weight events."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"The dashboard displays active lots and pens, animal counts by lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting versus current weight, weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain/FCR, cost per unit of gain, and energy consumed."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can inspect and compare lots, pens, rations, inventory, and feeding reports to identify highest feed consumption, best and worst lot FCR, highest ADG, most-used ration, plan variances, over- or underfeeding, remaining inventory, and cost per gain."},{"kind":"happy","text":"A yard-level summary aggregates active-lot head count, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost; users can drill from aggregate values into permitted underlying records."},{"kind":"data","text":"Views use the latest valid recorded data and identify unavailable metrics where inputs are incomplete; empty data sets show an empty state rather than fabricated results."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users only see operational records and details allowed by their access; unauthorized users cannot use dashboard or report views to expose restricted lot, pen, or cost information."}],"id":"I-8","readingChosen":"Treat dashboards and reports as role-permitted, filterable operational views over lot, pen, ration, inventory, feeding, and performance records."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A user views a lot comparison of ADG, FCR, and cost of gain and filters results by date range, breed, sex, and pen; changing a filter updates the displayed comparison."},{"kind":"happy","text":"A user exports the currently filtered report as CSV or PDF, and the downloaded file reflects the same selected lots, filters, and displayed metrics."},{"kind":"error","text":"If filters match no records, the report clearly shows no matching results and does not export unrelated lot data."},{"kind":"error","text":"Invalid date ranges or unsupported filter values are identified and not applied as valid report criteria."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users without report access cannot view or export restricted performance and financial data."}],"id":"I-9","readingChosen":"Treat the dedicated feed-to-gain report as a web-app report that compares lots and supports the listed filters and downloadable CSV or PDF files."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A user can load a coherent sample dataset containing procurement/receiving, lots, pens, inventory, rations, plans, feeding activities, and weight readings that supports dashboard and report demonstrations."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system labels sample records as mock/demo data and preserves their links across PO lines, lots, pens, and downstream activities so the demo can be traced end to end."},{"kind":"data","text":"Loading the same sample set again does not silently create duplicate source records; the user is told whether records were added, already present, or could not be loaded."},{"kind":"error","text":"If mock data conflicts with existing records or cannot be loaded, the system reports the affected records and does not present a partially loaded set as complete."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only users with permission to create demo data can load it; demo data is not represented as verified live procurement or animal information."}],"id":"I-10","readingChosen":"Treat sample/mock data as clearly labelled demo records that users can load to exercise the connected feedlot workflows without confusing it with live operational data."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A user can view a proposed solution overview and architecture diagrams describing the system's data flow and relationship between procurement, lots, pens, inventory, rations, feeding, weights, and analytics."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The demo area presents the app's workflow and sample-data demonstration, plus an overview of the prompts used, testing and validation performed, challenges encountered, and production-readiness assessment."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The area presents a go-to-market strategy and analysis for the feedlot management product, including its intended users and value proposition."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a requested diagram or evaluation section is unavailable, the app identifies that content as unavailable rather than implying it has been provided or validated."},{"kind":"data","text":"All pages, diagrams, reports, and demo interactions are usable in the responsive web app on phone, tablet, and desktop widths; touch controls remain usable at phone width."}],"id":"I-11","readingChosen":"Treat the requested proposal and evaluation materials as a project/demo area in the responsive web app, alongside the working feedlot workflows, rather than as separate native-app deliverables."}]},{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"An operator imports procurement and receiving records (PO line, vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, source); the system validates and stores accepted records and links them back to their source records."},{"kind":"data","text":"The operator maps a PO line to one or more lots, and maps lots to pens; the system preserves the PO-line → lot → pen links so users can trace lot and pen data back to procurement and receiving."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The system displays imported and mapped animal counts, weights, costs, pen capacity, and current counts so discrepancies can be identified."},{"kind":"error","text":"If required fields are missing, values are invalid, a source record cannot be matched, or a pen would exceed capacity, the system reports the affected records and does not silently create an invalid mapping."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a record is imported again, the system identifies duplicates and avoids silently double-counting animals, receipts, or costs."}],"id":"I-1"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"On receipt of animal/lot data, the system calculates and displays target weight and projected market/ship date for the lot using its entry weight, receiving date, target weight, and ADG assumption."},{"kind":"data","text":"Users can view the forecast inputs and update the target weight or ADG assumption; the displayed projection updates and the chosen assumptions are retained with the forecast."},{"kind":"error","text":"If entry weight, receiving date, target weight, or a usable ADG is missing or invalid, the system marks the forecast unavailable and identifies the missing input rather than presenting a misleading date."}],"id":"I-2","readingChosen":"Calculate forecasts from incoming entry weight and receiving date, using a configured target weight and ADG (or an explicitly selected default); present the assumptions with each projection."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can view feed items with category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry matter, energy, and storage location, plus opening stock, receipts, consumption, wastage, and closing stock."},{"kind":"data","text":"When feed is received, consumed, or adjusted, the system records a dated stock movement and updates the item's available and closing quantities and applicable cost totals."},{"kind":"data","text":"Users can set a wastage ratio; consumption estimates and projections include the configured wastage and show the ratio used."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can view inventory projections over daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons based on current stock, planned/recorded use, receipts, and wastage."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a movement would make available stock negative, units do not match, or required movement details are invalid, the system rejects or flags the movement and shows the resulting discrepancy instead of silently corrupting the balance."}],"id":"I-3"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can create and edit a ration with a name, type, intended animal/weight range, ingredients, and each ingredient's quantity or proportion."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system calculates the ration's ingredient proportions, dry matter, energy, and cost per unit from ingredient data and displays the resulting values with the ration."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can request a cost comparison/optimization by providing nutritional targets or constraints; the system presents feasible mixes and their estimated costs for comparison."},{"kind":"error","text":"If ingredient proportions do not total the required amount, an ingredient lacks cost/nutrition data, or constraints cannot be met, the system identifies the issue and does not save or present an invalid mix as optimized."}],"id":"I-4","readingChosen":"Treat optimization as comparing feasible ingredient mixes for lowest cost against user-specified nutritional targets/constraints; do not imply a guaranteed biological outcome."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can generate or edit a dated feeding plan for a pen using its animal count, bunk rate, selected ration, planned quantity, feeding time, and assigned lot(s); the plan shows per-animal quantity, estimated cost/energy, and status."},{"kind":"data","text":"Users can record actual feeding against a pen and plan, including date, lot, ration, planned and actual quantity, variance, and status; the system displays planned-versus-actual results."},{"kind":"data","text":"On saving a feeding activity, the system calculates variance as actual minus planned, calculates feed cost and energy from the ration, records ingredient consumption, and updates feed inventory and lot-level consumption/cost totals."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the pen, lot, ration, plan, or quantity is invalid or inventory is insufficient, the system reports the problem and does not silently post inconsistent consumption or costs."}],"id":"I-5"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can record a dated weight measurement for a lot, including number weighed, average weight, total lot weight, and notes; the system stores it as a new reading."},{"kind":"data","text":"The lot's weight history is displayed as a time series, including measurement dates and values, so users can inspect changes over time."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system calculates weight gain since the previous valid reading and makes the reading available to lot performance calculations."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the measurement date or weights are invalid, the animal count is inconsistent, or a reading predates the previous reading, the system flags the entry and avoids silently creating a misleading time series."}],"id":"I-6"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"For each lot, the system calculates days on feed from receiving date, total weight gain from current versus entry average weight, and ADG from gain divided by days on feed."},{"kind":"data","text":"The system calculates total feed consumed from saved feeding events, FCR as total feed consumed divided by total weight gain, and cost of gain as total feed cost divided by total weight gain."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The system projects ship date from current weight, target weight, days on feed, and ADG, and displays the inputs/values used for the projection."},{"kind":"data","text":"When a feeding event is saved or corrected, the system updates feed consumed, feed cost, FCR, and cost of gain for affected lots; when a weight event is saved or corrected, it updates gain, ADG, FCR, cost of gain, and projected ship date."},{"kind":"error","text":"If receiving date, entry/current weight, feed events, target weight, or a positive gain/ADG is unavailable, the affected metric is shown as unavailable with the reason; the system does not divide by zero or show a fabricated projection."}],"id":"I-7","readingChosen":"Use recorded actual feed delivered as feed consumed for the stated total-feed formula; calculate gain from lot average weights, and show metrics as unavailable when a required denominator or baseline is absent or zero."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can view dashboards and reports for active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, planned versus actual feeding, feed consumption/cost, weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain/FCR, cost of gain, and energy consumed."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can inspect lot- and pen-level results and identify best/worst performing lots, highest-consuming pens, most-used rations, feeding variances, and remaining inventory."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The dashboard presents a yard-level aggregate of active animals, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost when data is available."},{"kind":"error","text":"If source data or events are missing, the relevant metric is marked unavailable or clearly qualified rather than treated as zero or included without indication."}],"id":"I-8"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can open a dedicated feed-to-gain report comparing lots by ADG, FCR, and cost of gain."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can filter the report by date range, breed, sex, and pen; the displayed comparison updates to match the selected filters."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can export the currently filtered report as CSV or PDF, with the selected scope and metric values represented in the downloaded file."},{"kind":"error","text":"If filters produce no matching records or a requested metric cannot be calculated, the report indicates that condition and does not substitute misleading values."}],"id":"I-9"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"The system provides sample/mock procurement, receiving, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, and weight data that users can use to explore dashboards and calculations."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Mock records retain consistent links among PO lines, lots, pens, feed items, rations, plans, activities, and weight readings so the sample workflows and traceability can be demonstrated."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The interface identifies sample/mock data as such so users do not mistake it for live operational records."}],"id":"I-10"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"The solution presents a proposed approach and architecture diagrams showing the system's main data flows and relationships, including procurement/receiving through lots and pens to feeding, inventory, weights, and reporting."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Users can access a working web-app demo of the principal workflows and views, usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The solution presents an overview of testing and validation, including how feed-to-gain calculations and inventory/weight updates were checked, and identifies known challenges or limitations."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The solution states a production-readiness assessment, including material gaps or risks, and presents a go-to-market strategy and analysis for the product offering."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a demo workflow or calculation cannot be exercised because required sample data or inputs are absent, the demo identifies the missing dependency rather than implying the workflow succeeded."}],"id":"I-11"}]}]}